## What I Want From Extracts

<!-- How should the Executive Summary talk to you? -->
- Challenge my assumptions — if the source contradicts my approach, say so
- Be direct, no fluff. If the source is mediocre, say it's mediocre
- Connect to my current priorities where genuine
- Actionable implications over theoretical interest

## Value Scale

<!-- How a 1-10 rating maps to YOUR bar. The extractor uses this as the single source of truth for ratings — keep it, or tune the thresholds. -->
- 1-3 — low value, obvious, or wrong
- 4-5 — useful, some points worth keeping (most sources land here)
- 6 — changes one concrete decision or gives a usable tactic
- 7 — shifts a mental model / how you think about a domain (should be rare)
- 8-9 — reshapes your approach AND immediately actionable
- 10 — reference-grade, exceptional

<!-- Tend critical. 7+ should be rare. Don't drift to a comfortable middle. -->

